# QResP — Quantum-Resilient Provenance Audit

> Phase I of *Quantum-Resilient Provenance for Machine Learning Supply Chains*
> (CS F376 Design Project, BITS Pilani Dubai Campus, 2025–26).
> Supervisor: Dr. Tamizharasan Periyasamy.

`qresp` is a command-line tool that audits the cryptographic provenance of
public machine learning models on HuggingFace and classifies each one by
quantum vulnerability. It produces a reproducible JSON Lines dataset that
forms the empirical foundation of the project.

## What it does, in plain terms

The tool walks the HuggingFace registry, finds signature files attached to
each model (if any), parses them, identifies the underlying signature
algorithm, and tags the model with one of five labels:

| Label        | Meaning                                                       |
|--------------|---------------------------------------------------------------|
| `safe`       | Uses a post-quantum signature scheme (ML-DSA or SLH-DSA)      |
| `vulnerable` | Uses RSA, ECDSA, Ed25519 — broken by Shor's algorithm         |
| `unsigned`   | No signature file present at all                              |
| `mixed`      | Multiple signatures with disagreeing labels                   |
| `error`      | Signature present but could not be parsed (kept for review)   |

The tool **never downloads model weights**. It downloads only the signature
files themselves (typically kilobytes), so a full 1000-model scan is cheap
and fast.

## Installation

Requires Python 3.10 or newer.

```bash
git clone <repo-url>
cd qresp
pip install -e .
```

For analysis notebooks and figure generation:

```bash
pip install -e ".[analysis]"
```

For development (tests, linter, type checker):

```bash
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

## Usage

### Run a pilot scan on 50 models

```bash
qresp scan --n 50 --out data/pilot.jsonl
```

### Run the full audit on 1000 models

```bash
qresp scan --n 1000 --out data/full.jsonl
```

If your shell exports `HF_TOKEN`, the tool will pick it up automatically and
benefit from higher API rate limits.

### Summarise an existing dataset

```bash
qresp summarise --in data/pilot.jsonl
```

### Resume an interrupted scan

The scanner writes one JSON record per line as soon as each model is processed.
If the run is interrupted, just re-run the same command. Already-audited models
are skipped automatically. Pass `--no-resume` to start over.

